ering out other  universes controlling morty and  manipulating his conception and the  complete revenge field backstory of rick  with the company of a synthwave  soundtrack was magnificent  the only flaw here is that it feels like  the creators are uninterested in  devoting a lot of time for canon and  backstory so they opted to do a big dump  in the span of five minutes  and this issue connects back to the flaw  of pacing in that this evil morty arc  and backstory extravaganza takes place  in just 13 minutes  that's pretty wild and right after  watching it i felt like i needed a  re-watch because of how fast it ran  through the material  i wish the writer spent the whole  episode on this area instead of tying up  loose ends from the episode prior and  doing a samurai jack parody  they could have easily saved this parody  concept for another episode but throwing  it into this finale feels like they're  overloading it a bit  besides that flaw i don't feel like it's  enough to really discount the quality of  the finale the climax was epic and i  especially like the evolved and more  layered version of evil morty's theme  it all comes together in a bombastic  finale and you're left speechless as to  what just happened  it's just a shame that it could have  been as good as the reclantus mix-up had  the episode of devoted all of its time  to the evil morty arc  it's crazy how we can have episodes that  are easy contenders for the top 10 best  episodes in the series and then others  that easily make it into the worst  i just hope for season 6 that they can  make the quality between episodes more  consistent but if they don't then at  least we will probably get some bangers  at the end of the season if you enjoyed  the video let me know in the comments  and i can also do an episode ranking of  the other four seasons of rick and morty
 

